The section itself envisages three circumstances under which the inherent jurisdiction may be exercised,
namely, (i) to give effect to an order under the Code; (ii) to prevent abuse of the process of court;
and (iii) to otherwise secure the ends of justice.

Ordinarily and in the normal course, the High Court when approached for quashing of a criminal proceeding will not appreciate the defence of the accused;
Dheeraj Kumar Gera vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 14 December, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/114129682/
